<BaseLayout title="About — Raashid Arquil" description="Independent developer building my own products, and websites and apps for others."><div class="shell">
<header class="page-intro compact-intro"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1 class="display">The person<br/><em class="serif">behind the work.</em></h1></header>
<section class="about-grid revised-about"><aside><div class="portrait-frame"><OptimizedImage src="/images/profile.jpg" alt="Raashid Arquil" width="360" height="450" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 110px, 310px" loading="eager"/></div><p class="identity-name">Raashid Arquil</p><p class="small-copy">Independent developer · Working remotely</p><dl class="facts"><div><dt class="eyebrow">Education</dt><dd>B.Sc. (Hons) Computer Science<br/>First Class · Kingston University</dd></div><div><dt class="eyebrow">Also studied</dt><dd>PG Diploma, Professional Marketing<br/>CIM Level 7 · Merit<br/>Distinctions in two modules</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link mt-6" href="/resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a></aside>
<div class="article-body"><p>I build websites and mobile apps: my own products, and for people who need a developer to help with their situation. I've graduated, but I've still got a lot to learn, and I'm learning it by building.</p><p>I care that the software has a purpose. Before deciding what to build, I want to understand what someone is trying to do, what is difficult, and whether software can help.</p><p>Sometimes the starting point is personal. KeepClose came from forgetting people I don't meet often. SmartDrive came from the calls, books, and queues I dealt with while getting my driving licence.</p><h2>How I work</h2><p>I define the scope and user flows, research technical choices, and refine the implementation. I use AI throughout development, including implementation. It helps me move quickly; understanding the result and its limitations remains part of the work.</p><p>Right now I'm building KeepClose, CropCare, and Tally, and collaborating with another developer on a Next.js platform application. I'm taking on freelance projects, and I'm open to remote and hybrid engineering roles.</p><h2>Outside the build</h2><p>CropCare reached the Top 20 and then the Top 10 through Ascentic's AI Launchpad. I presented the MVP at TRACE, Sri Lanka, on 19 September 2026. <a href="https://ascentic.se/ailaunchpad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Programme and finalists ↗</a></p><p>At the ESOFT Intercampus Hackathon on 14 October 2023, I was part of Tech Titans, a team of five. I helped with research and worked on the Figma prototype for eHab, a mental-health support concept. We won the Software Engineering category. <a href="https://esoft.lk/esoft-events/tech-geniuses-shine-at-esoft-inter-campus-hackathon-2023/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Event overview ↗</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/notes/">Notes from these experiences ↗</a></div>
</section><ContactBanner/>
</div></BaseLayout>
